! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.58 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.65) --
! THE DISPATCHER'S TWO RETURNS.
!
! Thirty-two compiled lines out of forty-two: lines 5-6 and 12-41.
! Lines 1-4, 7-11 and 42 are comment rows, and lines 8-10 box the
! page's one heading, "ERROR RETURN ROUTINE".
!
! >>> THIS IS THE PAGE THE BOOT RUN WAS WAITING FOR. <<<
!
! Until 2026-10-24 the run ended by branching into zeroed storage at
! 003237.40, which decks/mcp_bootstrap_p54.strap calls
! "L NORM  SYN,(8)3237.40" -- a stand-in for a symbol whose page had
! not been transcribed.  THIS IS LINE 5 OF THAT PAGE, and the SYN is
! confirmed to the bit.  See docs/NEXT.md: the run reached it only
! once a VFL store was allowed to cross a word boundary, which let
! MCP read "IOD" off its configuration card instead of "I".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Two exits from the same dispatcher, and the listing names them in
! its own comments:
!
!   L NORM  (003237.40)  "-SWAP 8 INDICES." then
!                        "-DISPATCHER NORMAL RETURN."
!   L ERROR (003241.00)  the ERROR RETURN ROUTINE, which zeroes this
!                        program's IOREQ and FREEL slots, sets the
!                        reject bit, steps the PPREF index, and ends
!                        at "-DISPATCHER ERROR RETURN."
!
! BOTH RETURN THROUGH $15 AND THEY DIFFER BY A HALF WORD: line 6 is
! "B,2.0($15)" and line 41 is "B,1.32($15)".  A caller therefore
! plants a two-word linkage and the callee picks the arm.  That is
! the same shape printed p.43 line 54 uses ("B,1.32($15)" to return
! from S CA6), which is why the conversion routine and the dispatcher
! can share a convention without sharing code.
!
! AND THE TWO ENDS OF THE PAGE ARE THE SAME INSTRUCTION.  Line 5 and
! line 39 are both "SWAPI,8,L TY,L IODX" and both compile to
! 002571.00 80 000023.20 E0, to the bit.  The error path rejoins the
! normal path's index restore and then takes the other return.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> SIXTEEN STAND-INS CONFIRMED FROM THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every symbol below marked (confirmed) was given a value by an
! EARLIER deck, from a DIFFERENT page, before this page was read.
! Each was re-derived here from p.58's printed binary alone -- the
! index number out of an opcode byte's low nibble, the bit offset out
! of a location's octal pair -- and every one agreed:
!
!   L TY    (8)2571.0   line 5's first group, 002571.00
!   L IODX  $3          line 5's second group, 000023 = word 0o23
!   L XPP   $4          line 14's opcode 14, low nibble 4
!   L XIO   $5          line 27's ".12" -> bits 19-22 = 0101
!   L XFR   $6          line 28's ".14" -> bits 19-22 = 0110
!   L XNT   $9          line 23's "SC,L XNT,L XNT": the ADDRESS is
!                       000031 = word 0o31 = 16+9, and the J field
!                       ".23" is 1001.  The one row that pins an
!                       index register two ways at once.
!   L WORKX $10         line 25's opcode low nibble A
!   L FINB  (BU,1) (8)2601.51   line 12's first group
!   L OVBIT (BU,1) (8)2601.62   line 37's first group
!   L SAVEY (8)2603.0   line 27
!   L SAVEZ (8)2604.0   line 28
!   L NOSAV (8)2720.0   line 38's first group
!   T UNCT  (BU,8) 0.28 line 16's ".34" = 0o34 = 28
!   T LPPEN 0.39        lines 31 and 35's ".47" = 0o47 = 39
!   L NORM  (8)3237.40  line 5's own location -- DEFINED HERE
!   L ERROR (8)3241.0   line 12's own location -- DEFINED HERE
!
! THE LAST TWO ARE THE POINT.  printed p.54 SYNs both, and this page
! PLACES both from its own location counter.  mcp_image.py's merge
! turns each from a stand-in into a checked definition.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIVE SYMBOLS ARE NEW, and every one is derived here
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   L SAVE  (8)2602.0   lines 13 and 36 are "SX,L XNT,L SAVE" and
!                       "LX,L XNT,L SAVE" -- the save and the restore
!                       of one index, at the SAME address 002602,
!                       differing only in bit 23.  A pair like that
!                       cannot be a misreading of one row.
!   T IOREQ (8)3373.0   line 21
!   T LAST  0.18        line 20's ".22" = 0o22 = 18
!   T RJECT 0.37        line 30's ".45" = 0o45 = 37
!   LASTPP  (8)2613.0   line 33
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ".22" MEANS THREE DIFFERENT THINGS ON THIS PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 19, 20, 24, 25 and 29 all print ".22" in their first address
! group, and it is NOT the same field three of those times:
!
!   line 19  LX,L XNT,0.0(L WORKX)   -- the J FIELD: bits 19-22 of
!            ".22" = 010010 are 1001 = 9 = L XNT, and the modifying
!            index is in the opcode byte's low nibble (1A -> 10).
!   line 20  BZB,T LAST(L WORKX)     -- a BIT ADDRESS: 0o22 = 18,
!            which is T LAST's own offset.
!   lines 24, 25, 29  Z,0.0(index)   -- CONSTANT.  All three print
!            000000.22 and differ ONLY in the opcode byte (09, 0A,
!            04 = L XNT, L WORKX, L XPP), so the index is carried
!            there and ".22" belongs to the operation.
!
! Written down because the first reading of lines 24-25 tried to make
! ".22" an index field and could not: two rows whose statements name
! DIFFERENT index registers print the SAME ".22".  The opcode byte is
! what separates them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TYPOGRAPHY -- listing_typography.md 13 and 13e
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The scan prints digit zero with a gap at the right, so a leading 0
! reads as C.  In the SIX-DIGIT OCTAL fields that is never ambiguous
! -- octal has no C -- so "CC2571", "C03253" and "C0CC31" are
! 002571, 003253 and 000031 without a decision being made.
!
! THE HEX BYTES ARE WHERE A DECISION IS MADE, and three were:
!   line 21's "C1" is 01, settled by printed p.57 line 25, which is
!     the SAME statement ("LVI,L WORKX,T IOREQ") and the same
!     003373.25 01.
!   line 25's "CA" is 0A and line 29's "C4" is 04, settled by line
!     24's "09": all three are "Z,0.0(index)" and the opcode's high
!     nibble cannot change between them.
!   line 17's "C6" IS A C, and that is the counter-instance -- an
!     indicator branch, the same byte printed p.38 lines 30, 33, 38
!     and 40 carry.  A page that has three zeros-read-as-C also has
!     a C that is a C.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LAST LINE IS PINNED BY THE NEXT PAGE, four for four
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 41 is "B,1.32($15)" at 003264.00, one half word, and printed
! p.59 line 1 is "003264.40 *  SLC,$".  It lands exactly.  (Here the
! last line is an INSTRUCTION, whose length its own single printed
! code group already fixes, so this is corroboration rather than the
! only evidence -- unlike pp.42, 44 and 46, where the last row was a
! datum and the next page's SLC was the only thing holding it.)
!
! TWO LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location: lines 12
! ("003241.00 *") and 31 ("003254.40 *").  Same mark every page since
! printed p.3 carries; it compiles nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE GAVE T LPPEN A dds IT HAD NOT NEEDED BEFORE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Thirty of these thirty-two rows were bit-exact on the first run.
! The two that were not are lines 31 and 35, and both failed the same
! way: 000000 where the listing prints 001000 in the SECOND group --
! the FIELD LENGTH.
!
! THE DIFFERENCE IS THAT THIS PAGE WRITES THE OPERATION BARE.
! printed p.53 and printed p.57 only ever write
! "CM1111(BU,1),T LPPEN(L XPP)", with the dds on the statement, so
! T LPPEN's own dds never had to exist and p.53's SYN carried none.
! Lines 31 and 35 here are "CM0000,T LPPEN(L XPP)" and
! "CM1111,T LPPEN(L XPP)" -- nothing on the statement at all -- and a
! bare VFL statement takes its OPERAND SYMBOL'S dds.  C22-6531
! printed p.31 is the sentence: "THE MEANING OF SYN IS ALWAYS ONE OF
! EXACT SUBSTITUTION.  Thus, data properties (dds) associated with Y
! and its bit address or integer classification are transferred to
! A."
!
! SO T LPPEN IS SYN(BU,1), AND THE LISTING IS WHAT SAYS SO -- line
! 30's "CM1111(BU,1),T RJECT(L XPP)" and line 35's bare
! "CM1111,T LPPEN(L XPP)" print the SAME second group, 001000.36 F0,
! one page apart from each other in style and one line apart in fact.
! A one-bit flag called "the LPPEN BIT" having a one-bit dds is also
! the only thing it could sensibly be, but that is the weaker
! argument and it is not the one used.
!
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p53.strap was given the same SYN(BU,1) in the
! same commit: mcp_image.merge accepts two identical SYNs as a
! stand-in confirmed by its definition, and two that DISAGREE are a
! hard failure, so the pair has to move together.  p.53 is still
! bit-exact with it.

        SLC, (8)3237.40

! ---- stand-ins confirmed by this page (see header) ----------------
LIODX   SYN, $3
LXPP    SYN, $4
LXIO    SYN, $5
LXFR    SYN, $6
LXNT    SYN, $9
LWORKX  SYN, $10
LTY     SYN, (8)2571.0
LFINB   SYN(BU,1), (8)2601.51
LOVBIT  SYN(BU,1), (8)2601.62
LSAVEY  SYN, (8)2603.0
LSAVEZ  SYN, (8)2604.0
LNOSAV  SYN, (8)2720.0
TLPPEN  SYN(BU,1), 0.39
TUNCT   SYN(BU,8), 0.28
! ---- new on this page ---------------------------------------------
LSAVE   SYN, (8)2602.0
LASTPP  SYN, (8)2613.0
TIOREQ  SYN, (8)3373.0
TLAST   SYN(BU,1), 0.18
TRJECT  SYN(BU,1), 0.37

        SLC, (8)3237.40

! ---- the dispatcher's NORMAL return -------------------------------
LNORM   SWAPI, 8, LTY, LIODX         ! line 5  -SWAP 8 INDICES.
        B, 2.0($15)                  ! line 6  -DISPATCHER NORMAL
                                      !           RETURN.

! ---- the ERROR RETURN ROUTINE -------------------------------------
LERROR  CM1111(BU,1), LFINB, 0.0     ! line 12 -SET FINAL BIT TO 1.
        SX, LXNT, LSAVE              ! line 13 -SAVE INDEX.
        LX, LWORKX, 0.0(LXPP)        ! line 14 -SET IOREQ AND FREEL
                                      !           SLOTS FOR
        BXVZZ, LERR2                 ! line 15 -  THIS PROGRAM TO
                                      !           ZERO.
        L, TUNCT(LXPP), 46           ! line 16
        BRZZ, LERR2                  ! line 17
        LC, LWORKX, $R               ! line 18
LERRA   LX, LXNT, 0.0(LWORKX)        ! line 19
        BZB, TLAST(LWORKX), LERR3    ! line 20 -END OF IOREQ TABLE
        LVI, LWORKX, TIOREQ          ! line 21
LERR3   BXCZZ, LERR1                 ! line 22
        SC, LXNT, LXNT               ! line 23
        Z, 0.0(LXNT)                 ! line 24 -ZERO FREEL SLOT.
LERR1   Z, 0.0(LWORKX)               ! line 25 -ZERO IOREQ SLOT.
        CB+, LWORKX, LERRA           ! line 26 -BACK ON NON-ZERO
                                      !           COUNT.
        LX, LXIO, LSAVEY             ! line 27 -RESET THE IOREQ INDEX
        LX, LXFR, LSAVEZ             ! line 28 -RELOAD THE FREEL
                                      !           TABLE INDEX
LERR2   Z, 0.0(LXPP)                 ! line 29 -ZERO PPREF SLOT.
        CM1111(BU,1), TRJECT(LXPP)   ! line 30 -SET THE REJECT BIT
        CM0000, TLPPEN(LXPP)         ! line 31 -RESET THIS LPPEN BIT
        SC, 15, $R                   ! line 32 -ERROR FLAG TO ACC
        SX, LXPP, LASTPP             ! line 33 -SAVE ADR. OF LAST PP
                                      !           ENTERED
        V+ICR, LXPP, 2.0             ! line 34 -STEP PPREF INDEX.
        CM1111, TLPPEN(LXPP)         ! line 35 -SET THE NEXT LPPEN
                                      !           BIT
        LX, LXNT, LSAVE              ! line 36 -RESTORE INDEX.
        BZBZ, LOVBIT, LERR4          ! line 37 -IF OVERLAP MODE
        SWAPI, 3, LNOSAV, LXPP       ! line 38 -RESET INDEXES TO
                                      !           OVERLAP MODE
LERR4   SWAPI, 8, LTY, LIODX         ! line 39 -SWAP 8 INDEXES
        SC, $15, 1.0($15)            ! line 40 -SAVE THE ERROR FLAG
        B, 1.32($15)                 ! line 41 -DISPATCHER ERROR
                                      !           RETURN.
        END, LNORM

